    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d42">

                <pb facs="0335" n="21" sameAs="frus:frus1914Supp/pg21"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/27</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Vice Consul at Kingston, Jamaica</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Bundy</hi>), <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Consulate</hi>, <lb/>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Kingston</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1914-07-30T16:00:00-05:00">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">July 30, 1914, 4 p.m.</hi>
                    </date>
                    <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 7:35 p.m.</hi>] </dateline>
                <p rendition="#center">[Telegram]</p>
                <p>Jamaica forts manned, regiments hurried to Kingston to-day.<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d42-f1"/> German cruiser <hi rendition="#italic">Dresden</hi>
                    cruising off three-mile limit. Governor has suppressed all the reports
                    pertaining to military operations. Official report not verified.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bundy</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d42-f1" n="1" xml:id="d42-f1-content">
                <p>For further information regarding British military and naval preparations of this
                    date, see the consular despatches from Georgetown (British Guiana), Cardiff, and
                    Cork, which reached the Department on August 14, <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >post</hi>, <ref target="#pg56">pp. 56</ref>, <ref target="#pg57">57</ref>,
                        <ref target="#pg58">58</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
